<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="leo_model1_cad">

  <!-- ============================================================
       Leo Rover Model 1 (leo1_model, FLIR+SPAD chassis) — v2, rebuilt
       from the post-material-fix CAD link property sheet
       (Leo_Rover_CAD_Link_Properties.xlsx).

       *** CHANGES FROM v1 ***
       - Mass/CoM/inertia updated for every link from the new sheet.
       - Fixed the double-offset bug: v1 applied a joint-origin
         translation on top of mesh vertices that were ALREADY
         expressed in the shared CAD assembly frame, so every child
         link's geometry was displaced twice. All <visual> and
         <collision> blocks below now carry a compensating <origin>
         equal to -(that link's own CAD pivot position), which
         re-centers the mesh into its own link frame. wheel_FR/RR
         reuse the FL/RL mesh files verbatim, so their compensation
         uses the SOURCE mesh's pivot (FL's / RL's), not their own —
         the joint chain handles moving the reused shape to the
         right/rear position; the visual origin only undoes what's
         already baked into that specific mesh file.
       - Joint rotation axes changed from (0 1 0) to (1 0 0). The
         sheet's "Axis of Revolution" column says x for every rocker
         and wheel joint, and this sheet's X axis is confirmed
         (large ~130-224mm magnitudes, sign-flipped between L/R) to
         be the left-right/track-width axis — consistent with what a
         wheel physically needs to rotate about. v1 used axis (0 1 0),
         which appears to have been wrong under this frame; verify
         this resolves any odd rolling behavior you may have seen.
       - Collision box dimensions carried over from v1 have their
         X/Y swapped (e.g. rocker box 0.0812x0.3339 -> 0.3339x0.0812)
         to match this axis relabeling. These are still placeholder
         boxes (see flag on collision geometry below) — the swap
         keeps them physically sensible, it doesn't re-derive them.
       - Colors added per-link (see <material> defs below).

       *** STILL OPEN / NEW FLAGS — READ BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE ***
       1) AXIS CONVENTION: this file uses the CAD sheet's x/y/z axes
          directly and consistently (verified via a mesh-bbox-vs-pivot
          spot check on rocker_L, and the axis="x" rotation note
          above). It has NOT been checked against ROS REP-103
          (X-forward, Y-left, Z-up) — the sheet's axes may not match
          that convention. If downstream nodes (nav, teleop) assume
          REP-103, you likely need a fixed rotation at the root, not
          another edit to these joint origins.
       2) rocker_R_link inertia looks inconsistent with rocker_L,
          beyond the known ~7mm pivot mismatch (flagged previously,
          still present: rocker_L pivot x=130.187mm vs rocker_R
          x=-123.187mm). The two parts should be near-mirror-images
          with similar inertia MAGNITUDES, but rocker_R's Iyy
          (243,300) and Izz (3,120,000) are roughly 40x and 4x
          smaller than rocker_L's (9,903,000 / 12,410,000) — not
          just a sign/mirroring difference. Worth re-checking this
          row in the CAD before trusting rocker_R's dynamics.
       3) camera_frame's inertia tensor as given is NOT symmetric:
          the sheet's Ixz column (1,974,000) does not match its Izx
          column (21,490,000), and Iyz (6,021,000) does not match
          Izy (24,120,000) — every other link's sheet row is
          internally symmetric. This file uses the Ixz/Iyz values
          below; please verify against the sheet/CAD directly, since
          I can't tell which pair is the transcription error.
       4) wheel_FR_link / wheel_RR_link have NO dedicated sheet row —
          their pivot, CoM, and inertia below are DERIVED by
          mirroring wheel_FL/wheel_RL's data across the rocker_R
          side (sign-flip the left-right axis, keep fore-aft/vertical
          the same), not independently measured. Reasonable given the
          reused mesh, but flagging since it's inference, not sheet
          data.
       5) Total assembled mass is now ~13.7 kg (vs. Fictionlab's
          ~6.5-7kg spec) — much better than v1's ~30kg, and
          camera_frame dropping from 17.6kg to 4.16kg strongly
          suggests the material-assignment fix worked. Still roughly
          2x spec, though, so camera_frame (4.16kg) in particular may
          be worth a second look before trusting dynamics.
       6) camera_frame still has no separate CAD mount pivot (sheet
          gives only a CoM), so it remains wired as a FIXED joint to
          base_link at its own CoM position, per v1's approach.
       7) Collision geometry still uses full visual meshes are NOT
          used here (boxes are), but the box dimensions themselves
          are still v1's rough placeholders (axis-swapped, not
          re-measured) — base_link, camera_frame, and the wheel
          meshes were flagged as non-watertight previously; that is
          unchanged.
       8) v3: wheel_FR_link / wheel_RR_link now mirror the FL/RL mesh
          via a negative X scale on the <mesh> tag, rather than just
          translating it — see the comment on each link. This is a
          geometric best-effort based on the established axis
          convention (X = left-right), but I have not visually
          verified it against the actual STL geometry — please check
          in Gazebo that the wheels now look correctly oriented
          (hub/tread facing outward on both sides) and that the boxy
          collision geometry still roughly encloses each wheel.
  ============================================================ -->

  <material name="chassis_light_gray">
    <!-- Approximate match for Leo Rover's chassis color — no exact
         swatch reference was available; adjust if you have one. -->
    <color rgba="0.80 0.80 0.80 1.0"/>
  </material>
  <material name="running_gear_black">
    <color rgba="0.05 0.05 0.05 1.0"/>
  </material>
  <material name="camera_green">
    <color rgba="0.10 0.55 0.20 1.0"/>
  </material>

  <!-- ============ base_link (root) ============ -->
  <link name="base_link">
    <visual>
      <!-- No compensating origin: base_link IS the robot's own frame
           origin (pivot_global = 0,0,0 by definition), so the mesh
           is trusted as-is. -->
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_base_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="chassis_light_gray"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.011280 0.015301 -0.011655" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.3110 0.2831 0.0981"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.011280 0.015301 -0.011655" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.987750"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.015760000" ixy="-0.001661000" ixz="0.000289200"
               iyy="0.011790000" iyz="0.001192000" izz="0.024350000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ rocker_L_link ============ -->
  <joint name="rocker_L_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rocker_L_link"/>
    <origin xyz="0.130187 -0.001011 0.016361" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="rocker_L_link">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.130187 0.001011 -0.016361" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_rocker_L_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.292827 0.000001 -0.048915" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.3339 0.0812 0.1341"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.292827 0.000001 -0.048915" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.351114"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.003541000" ixy="-0.000057698" ixz="-0.001796000"
               iyy="0.009903000" iyz="-0.000011971" izz="0.012410000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ rocker_R_link (see flag #2: inertia looks off vs rocker_L) ============ -->
  <joint name="rocker_R_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rocker_R_link"/>
    <origin xyz="-0.123187 -0.001017 0.016361" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="rocker_R_link">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.123187 0.001017 -0.016361" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_rocker_R_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.285827 0.000006 -0.048915" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.3339 0.0812 0.1341"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.285827 0.000006 -0.048915" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.351114"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.003078000" ixy="-0.000000001" ixz="-0.000063100"
               iyy="0.000243300" iyz="-0.000000007" izz="0.003120000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ wheel_FL_link ============ -->
  <joint name="wheel_FL_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="rocker_L_link"/>
    <child link="wheel_FL_link"/>
    <origin xyz="0.093819 -0.147764 -0.131244" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="wheel_FL_link">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.224006 0.148775 0.114883" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_wheel_FL_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.065122 0.000168 0.000549" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1300 0.1343 0.1300"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.065122 0.000168 0.000549" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.708924"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.001394000" ixy="0.000008954" ixz="0.000028970"
               iyy="0.002361000" iyz="0.000012759" izz="0.002397000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ wheel_RL_link ============ -->
  <joint name="wheel_RL_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="rocker_L_link"/>
    <child link="wheel_RL_link"/>
    <origin xyz="0.093819 0.147764 -0.131243" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="wheel_RL_link">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="-0.224006 -0.146753 0.114882" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_wheel_RL_link.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="-0.065122 -0.000177 0.000546" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1300 0.1343 0.1300"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.065122 -0.000177 0.000546" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.708924"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.001394000" ixy="-0.000009282" ixz="0.000028867"
               iyy="0.002361000" iyz="-0.000012712" izz="0.002397000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ wheel_FR_link (mirrored/derived — see flag #4) ============ -->
  <joint name="wheel_FR_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="rocker_R_link"/>
    <child link="wheel_FR_link"/>
    <origin xyz="-0.093819 -0.147764 -0.131244" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="wheel_FR_link">
    <visual>
      <!-- v3: true mirror via negative X scale, NOT a translated reuse
           of FL's mesh as-is. Without this, the wheel's hub asymmetry
           (or any other X-axial feature) points the wrong way on the
           right side. Because the geometry is now genuinely mirrored,
           the origin below uses wheel_FR's OWN pivot (not FL's) —
           different from the collision/inertial origin logic, which
           is unaffected since it's just a placeholder box. -->
      <origin xyz="0.217006 0.148781 0.114883" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_wheel_FL_link.stl" scale="-0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.065122 0.000168 0.000549" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1300 0.1343 0.1300"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.065122 0.000168 0.000549" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.708924"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.001394000" ixy="-0.000008954" ixz="-0.000028970"
               iyy="0.002361000" iyz="0.000012759" izz="0.002397000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ wheel_RR_link (mirrored/derived — see flag #4) ============ -->
  <joint name="wheel_RR_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="rocker_R_link"/>
    <child link="wheel_RR_link"/>
    <origin xyz="-0.093819 0.147764 -0.131243" rpy="0 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="wheel_RR_link">
    <visual>
      <!-- v3: true mirror via negative X scale — see wheel_FR_link's
           comment above for the full explanation. -->
      <origin xyz="0.217006 -0.146747 0.114882" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_wheel_RL_link.stl" scale="-0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="running_gear_black"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.065122 -0.000177 0.000546" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.1300 0.1343 0.1300"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.065122 -0.000177 0.000546" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.708924"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.001394000" ixy="0.000009282" ixz="-0.000028867"
               iyy="0.002361000" iyz="-0.000012712" izz="0.002397000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- ============ camera_frame (fixed mount, see flags 3 & 6) ============ -->
  <joint name="camera_frame_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="camera_frame"/>
    <origin xyz="-0.001737 0.030583 0.113168" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>
  <link name="camera_frame">
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.001737 -0.030583 -0.113168" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://leo_description_cad/meshes/cad/leo1_model_camera_frame.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="camera_green"/>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.000000 0.000000 0.000000" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <box size="0.2410 0.2260 0.2094"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0.000000 0.000000 0.000000" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="4.162364"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.024070000" ixy="-0.001500000" ixz="0.001974000"
               iyy="0.030050000" iyz="0.006021000" izz="0.094600000"/>
    </inertial>
  </link>

  <!-- No antenna_link: this CAD model (leo1_model) does not include an antenna component. -->

</robot>
